    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d515">

                <pb facs="0732" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg626"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ecuadorean Minister to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Ecuador</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1906-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                26, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: Confirming the agreeable
                    interview I had with your excellency I have the pleasure to repeat in this note
                    that I have received instructions from the foreign office at Quito to state how
                    much the Government and people of Ecuador regretted to be deprived of your
                    excellency’s visit on your recent trip to South America.</p>
                <p>My Government regrets that conditions beyond your excellency’s control prevented
                    your reaching Guayaquil, where Ecuador would have had the hoped-for opportunity
                    to express their high esteem for your excellency and for the great Republic
                    which you so worthily represent.</p>
                <p>I beg your excellency to be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. F. Carbo.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
